  "verdict": "Two axes \u2014 RANK confidence (rank_gap) and SUPPORT stability (manifold_support) \u2014 were combined in a logistic detector fit ONLY on train epochs and evaluated ONLY on held-out epochs inside the forced zone (base accuracy 0.175). Held-out forced-zone AUC for the main two-axis model: parity=0.8376, contiguous=0.8309 (chance 0.5). The detector SURVIVES held-out evaluation on both the charitable (parity) and adversarial (contiguous) epoch splits: at the train-selected operating point it lifts retained accuracy above the no-abstention base and captures more errors than correct rows it wrongly abstains. Abstention on probable FALSE COLLAPSE is operationally useful but NOT production-ready; sharpening/truncation remains hazardous because support breadth is part of the correctness signal."
